legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{4}","name":"Vedalken Orrery","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","oracle_text":"You may cast spells as though they had flash.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2022-07-08","toughness":null,"type_line":"Artifact"},{"oracle_id":"938b4e2c-88d9-4637-bc00-e228920c9a78","name":"Murder","mana_cost":"{1}{B}{B}","type_line":"Instant","oracle_text":"Destroy target creature.","power":null,"toughness":null,"loyalty":null,"defense":null,"colors":["B"],"color_identity":["B"],"keywords":[],"produced_mana":[],"layout":"normal","released_at":"2024-09-27","faces":[],"cmc":3.0,"legalities":{"alchemy":"legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"not_legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"}},{"oracle_id":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000651","name":"Generic Bound Plains","mana_cost":"","cmc":0,"type_line":"Basic Land — Plains","oracle_text":"({T}: Add {W}.)","colors":[],"color_identity":["W"],"keywords":[],"produced_mana":["W"],"layout":"normal","released_at":"2026-01-01","legalities":{"commander":"legal"}}],"rulings":[{"oracle_id":"162e45f5-edb8-4a13-acdc-8980ce5ba8ac","published_at":"2012-05-01","source":"wotc","comment":"If you control no other creatures, you won’t sacrifice anything."},{"oracle_id":"162e45f5-edb8-4a13-acdc-8980ce5ba8ac","published_at":"2012-05-01","source":"wotc","comment":"If Demonic Taskmaster leaves the battlefield after its ability triggers but before it resolves, you’ll still have to sacrifice a creature. Notably, if you control two Demonic Taskmasters and no other creatures, each one will force you to sacrifice the other."},{"oracle_id":"9ae669dd-7e60-4649-b96e-35da28be641a","published_at":"2019-10-04","source":"wotc","comment":"If you sacrifice a permanent as part of a spell or activated ability's cost, Korvold's last ability will resolve before that spell or ability."},{"oracle_id":"9ae669dd-7e60-4649-b96e-35da28be641a","published_at":"2019-10-04","source":"wotc","comment":"If you sacrifice Korvold, its last ability triggers. You won't put a +1/+1 counter on anything, but you'll draw a card."},{"oracle_id":"9ae669dd-7e60-4649-b96e-35da28be641a","published_at":"2019-10-04","source":"wotc","comment":"A legendary permanent that is put into a graveyard because of the \"legend rule\" isn't sacrificed."},{"oracle_id":"9ae669dd-7e60-4649-b96e-35da28be641a","published_at":"2019-10-04","source":"wotc","comment":"Korvold's last ability is a triggered ability, not an activated ability. It doesn't allow you to sacrifice a permanent whenever you want; rather, you need some other way of sacrificing permanents, such as Korvold's first triggered ability."},{"oracle_id":"9ae669dd-7e60-4649-b96e-35da28be641a","published_at":"2019-10-04","source":"wotc","comment":"If you somehow control no other permanents, you can attack with Korvold. You won't sacrifice anything, and there's no penalty for being unable to do so."},{"oracle_id":"ed3990cd-fa67-427b-bbe4-a2b1942e9be2","published_at":"2016-04-08","source":"wotc","comment":"In the unusual situation that you control no other creatures or lands, the last ability won't do anything. Morkrut Necropod can attack or block with no penalty."},{"oracle_id":"ed3990cd-fa67-427b-bbe4-a2b1942e9be2","published_at":"2016-04-08","source":"wotc","comment":"When Morkrut Necropod attacks, its trigger doesn't resolve until after all attackers have been chosen. The same is true for when it blocks. This means that another creature, such as one enchanted with Invocation of Saint Traft, can also attack or block and then be sacrificed. Sacrificing a blocking creature this way doesn't cause the creature it blocked to become unblocked."},{"oracle_id":"e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f","published_at":"2014-07-18","source":"wotc","comment":"Abilities that Slivers grant, as well as power/toughness boosts, are cumulative. However, for some abilities, like indestructible and the ability granted by Belligerent Sliver, having more than one instance of the ability doesn’t provide any additional benefit."},{"oracle_id":"e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f","published_at":"2014-07-18","source":"wotc","comment":"If you change the creature type of a Sliver you control so it’s no longer a Sliver, it will no longer be affected by its own ability. Its ability will continue to affect other Sliver creatures you control."},{"oracle_id":"e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f","published_at":"2014-07-18","source":"wotc","comment":"Slivers in this set affect only Sliver creatures you control. They don’t grant bonuses to your opponents’ Slivers. This is the same way Slivers from the Magic 2014 core set worked, while Slivers in earlier sets granted bonuses to all Slivers."},{"oracle_id":"e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f","published_at":"2014-07-18","source":"wotc","comment":"Damage dealt to a Sliver with indestructible is still marked on that creature. If it has lethal damage marked on it and it loses indestructible (perhaps because Sliver Hivelord leaves the battlefield), it will be destroyed."},{"oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc","comment":"When an effect returns the exiled card \"under your control,\" you control it indefinitely after that. In a multiplayer game, if a player leaves the game, all cards that player owns leave as well. If you leave the game, any creatures you control from Cloudshift's effect are exiled."},{"oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc","comment":"If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won't return to the battlefield."},{"oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc","comment":"Once the exiled permanent returns, it's considered a new object with no relation to the object that it was. Auras attached to the exiled permanent will be put into their owners' graveyards. Equipment attached to the exiled permanent will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled permanent will cease to exist."},{"oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc","comment":"The returned card won't be the target of any spells or abilities that targeted it before. Any spells that don't target, such as Akroma's Vengeance, will still affect it."},{"oracle_id":"8e0cea9c-3110-4728-9378-76849e33bb90","published_at":"2012-07-01","source":"wotc","comment":"If an attacking creature loses haste, perhaps because Fervor leaves the battlefield after attackers have been declared, it won't be removed from combat."},{"oracle_id":"8dc067bf-f78f-4ac4-b6e7-b305c42cf0bc","published_at":"2014-07-18","source":"wotc","comment":"Although Darksteel Citadel is an artifact, it can't be cast as a spell. Playing it follows the normal rules for playing a land."},{"oracle_id":"9d08af23-9f4a-4097-9abc-3b17475ab744","published_at":"2019-07-12","source":"wotc","comment":"Act of Treason can target any creature, even one that's untapped or one you already control."},{"oracle_id":"9d08af23-9f4a-4097-9abc-3b17475ab744","published_at":"2019-07-12","source":"wotc","comment":"Gaining control of a creature doesn't cause you to gain control of any Auras or Equipment attached to it."},{"oracle_id":"049d1fb2-cce7-40e7-a633-e84cf9782d89","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc","comment":"If you Donate an Aura, it stays where it is, but the targeted player now controls it."},{"oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","published_at":"2004-12-01","source":"wotc","comment":"The controller of Vedalken Orrery can cast nonland artifact, creature, enchantment, and sorcery cards any time they could cast an instant. This includes on other players' turns and during the upkeep step, draw step, combat phase, and end step."},{"oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","published_at":"2010-06-15","source":"wotc","comment":"This applies only to casting spells. It does not, for example, change when you may activate abilities that can only be activated \"any time you could cast a sorcery\"."}]}
